WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.860
Cut the right half of the spinal cord, at the tenth thoracic segment.

2
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.600
That is a hemisection at T10.

3
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.460
What is lost, and on which side?

4
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.920
The answer depends on where two pathways cross the midline.

5
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.860
Touch and pain enter through the same dorsal root.

6
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.860
Then they part company.

7
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:31.190
Fine touch, vibration and position sense travel by the dorsal column medial

8
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.370
lemniscus pathway.

9
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.810
The first axon enters the cord and climbs on the same side, in the dorsal column.

10
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.190
It does not synapse on the way.

11
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.550
It synapses in the gracile or cuneate nucleus, in the caudal medulla.

12
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.550
Axons from there cross the midline and climb to the thalamus, which relays to the

13
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.850
cortex. This pathway crosses in the medulla.

14
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.800
Pain and temperature travel by the spinothalamic pathway.

15
00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.680
The first axon synapses in the dorsal horn, near where it entered.

16
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.340
The second axon crosses the midline within a segment or two, through the anterior

17
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.440
white commissure. Then it climbs the opposite side of the cord to the thalamus.

18
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.580
This pathway crosses in the spinal cord.

19
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.640
Now make the cut, in the right half of the cord.

20
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.140
Touch fibres from the right side of the body have not crossed yet.

21
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.220
They climb in the right dorsal column, so the cut severs them.

22
00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.640
Pain fibres from the left side of the body have already crossed.

23
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.660
They climb in the right anterolateral cord, so the cut severs those too.

24
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:49.303
So fine touch, vibration and position sense are lost on the right, below T10.

25
00:01:50.403 --> 00:01:52.643
Pain and temperature are lost on the left.

26
00:01:53.343 --> 00:01:57.883
That loss begins a little lower, from about T11 to T12 down.

27
00:01:58.663 --> 00:02:01.483
Some fibres cross above the cut and escape it.

28
00:02:02.363 --> 00:02:04.023
Weakness is on the right as well.

29
00:02:04.743 --> 00:02:10.123
The corticospinal tract crossed in the caudal medulla, so in the cord it serves its

30
00:02:10.123 --> 00:02:11.123
own side.

31
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:16.637
Touch and strength are lost on one side, and pain on the other.

32
00:02:17.377 --> 00:02:19.417
That is the Brown-Séquard pattern.

33
00:02:20.357 --> 00:02:25.057
Both pathways are major routes, not the whole of touch or pain processing.

34
00:02:25.917 --> 00:02:28.797
Where each one crosses lets you locate a lesion.

35
00:02:29.697 --> 00:02:31.437
Fine touch crosses in the medulla.

36
00:02:32.337 --> 00:02:33.977
Pain crosses in the spinal cord.
